# What ships to pub.dev, and what does not.
#
# `.pubignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for publishing, so everything that must be
# kept out of the archive has to be named here — not just the things git also
# ignores.
#
# Measured: the archive carried 674 045 bytes (0.64 MB gzipped) of golden
# reference PNGs and internal audit prose that no consumer of the package can
# act on. None of it is reachable from `package:flutter_notemus`.

# --- Build and tool output (also in .gitignore) ---
.dart_tool/
.idea/
.vscode/
build/
*.iml
*.log
.DS_Store
.claude
.vercel
.playwright-cli/
linux/flutter/
temp_notemus_multiplatform/
temp_notemus_plugin/

# --- Ad-hoc measurement probes ---
# `probe/` is in `.gitignore`, which is exactly why it needs to be here: this
# file REPLACES `.gitignore` for publishing, so an untracked-but-not-ignored-
# here directory starts shipping the moment this file appears. Measured:
# adding this file without this line would have ADDED 0.61 MB gzipped of
# throwaway before/after comparison rasters to the archive.
probe/

# --- Golden reference images and their failure dumps ---
# These exist to be compared against by `flutter test --tags golden` IN THIS
# REPOSITORY. `matchesGoldenFile` is not portable across platforms — see
# `dart_test.yaml` — so a consumer cannot meaningfully run them, and 1.3 MB of
# PNGs would be downloaded by every app that depends on this package.
# The test SOURCE still ships; only the binary references do not.
test/golden/goldens/
test/golden/failures/

# --- Internal engineering record ---
# Kept in git, where it is auditable, and out of the package, where it is
# noise. The forensic audits, their superprompts and the running progress log
# are addressed to this project's maintainers, not to its users, and several
# are written in Portuguese.
PROGRESS.md
doc/AUDITORIA_*.md
doc/REAUDIT_SUPERPROMPT*.md
doc/PROGRESS_REPORT_*.md
doc/*_AUDIT_BACKLOG.md
doc/TECH_DEBT_*.md
doc/ARTICLE_HANDOFF.md
doc/OPEN_ISSUES.md

# Deliberately still shipped: doc/adr/ (the architectural decisions a consumer
# has to know to use the API correctly), doc/MODEL_ONLY.md, doc/MEI_V5_AUDIT.md,
# doc/json_schema.md, doc/MAGIC_NUMBERS_REFERENCE.md and the Gregorian design
# notes — all of them answer questions about the public surface.
